# Every text file checks out LF on every platform.
#
# text=auto, not bare text: auto keeps git's binary detection, so the png/jpg
# blobs are left alone. Bare `text` would mark them as text and corrupt them.
# Without an explicit eol, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) produced
# CRLF working-tree files while the blobs stayed LF, which broke every test
# fixture that string-matches on \n. See docs/harness-audit-2026-08.md mode 10.
* text=auto eol=lf
